                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239412297",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198049840197",
                            "num_reviews": 522,
                            "playtime_forever": 328,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 328,
                            "playtime_at_review": 328,
                            "last_played": 1793858397
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have very mixed feelings.\r\n\r\nOn one hand, I love Onimusha: Warlords. Its a great game, possibly the best (non Resident Evil) survival horror game to come out of Capcom in the PS2 era.\r\n\r\nOn the other, this port is pretty lazy. Models clip into each other, the shadows are messed up. The translation was not improved, the crap voice acting remains. They also made some baffeling changes to the controls, you can now play the game with full 8 direction movement using the left analogue stick. Or you can stick to traditional tank controls, so long as you only use the D-pad.\r\n\r\nIts quite awkward and annoying. I want traditional tank controls with my left stick, like what I had on the Ps2. \r\n\r\nI wish they had given the port job more work, cause this is a great game it just needs a little more tender love and care to justify the price. If you don't already own a PS2 and cannot get an emulator, this is an acceptable way to play I suppose.",
